    @section odbcschema Schema Introspection Functions

    The ODBC module provides functions for querying database schema metadata using ODBC catalog functions.

    @subsection odbc_schema_tables odbc_get_tables()

    Returns a list of tables in the database.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> tables = odbc_get_tables(ds);
    # With optional filters:
    list<hash<auto>> tables = odbc_get_tables(ds, catalog, schema, table_pattern, type);
    @endcode

    Each hash in the returned list contains: \c catalog, \c schema, \c name, \c type, \c remarks.

    @subsection odbc_schema_columns odbc_get_columns()

    Returns column metadata for a table.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> columns = odbc_get_columns(ds, "users");
    # With optional filters:
    list<hash<auto>> columns = odbc_get_columns(ds, "users", catalog, schema, column_pattern);
    @endcode

    Each hash contains: \c catalog, \c schema, \c table, \c name, \c type, \c type_name, \c size, \c decimal_digits, \c nullable, \c remarks, \c default, \c ordinal_position.

    @subsection odbc_schema_primary_keys odbc_get_primary_keys()

    Returns primary key information for a table.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> pk = odbc_get_primary_keys(ds, "users");
    @endcode

    Each hash contains: \c catalog, \c schema, \c table, \c column, \c key_seq, \c pk_name.

    @subsection odbc_schema_foreign_keys odbc_get_foreign_keys()

    Returns foreign key relationships for a table.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> fks = odbc_get_foreign_keys(ds, "orders");
    @endcode

    Each hash contains: \c pk_catalog, \c pk_schema, \c pk_table, \c pk_column, \c fk_catalog, \c fk_schema, \c fk_table, \c fk_column, \c key_seq, \c update_rule, \c delete_rule, \c fk_name, \c pk_name.

    @subsection odbc_schema_indexes odbc_get_indexes()

    Returns index information for a table.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> indexes = odbc_get_indexes(ds, "users");
    # Get only unique indexes:
    list<hash<auto>> unique_indexes = odbc_get_indexes(ds, "users", True);
    @endcode

    Each hash contains: \c catalog, \c schema, \c table, \c non_unique, \c index_name, \c type, \c ordinal_position, \c column, \c asc_or_desc, \c cardinality, \c pages.

    @subsection odbc_schema_procedures odbc_get_procedures()

    Returns stored procedures in the database.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> procs = odbc_get_procedures(ds);
    @endcode

    Each hash contains: \c catalog, \c schema, \c name, \c num_input_params, \c num_output_params, \c num_result_sets, \c remarks, \c type.

    @subsection odbc_schema_type_info odbc_get_type_info()

    Returns supported SQL data types.

    @code
    list<hash<auto>> types = odbc_get_type_info(ds);
    @endcode

    Each hash contains information about supported data types including \c type_name and \c data_type.

    @section odbcstoredprocs Stored Procedures

    Stored procedure execution is supported; the following is an example of a stored procedure call:

    Example PostgreSQL PLPG/SQL function:
    @code
create or replace function int_test(val int4) returns int4 as $$
begin
    return val * 2;
end;
$$ language plodbc;
    @endcode

    Example Qore code to call this function:
    @code
auto result = db.exec("select int_test(%v)", 11);
printf("%N\n", result);
    @endcode

    Resulting in:
    @verbatim
hash: (1 member)
  int_test : 22
    @endverbatim

    @section odbcreleasenotes Release Notes

    @subsection odbcv1_2_0 odbc Driver Version 1.2.0
    - added support for returning the ODBC driver name in \c Datasource::getDriverRealName()
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4690">issue 4690</a>)
    - added schema introspection functions: \c odbc_get_tables(), \c odbc_get_columns(),
      \c odbc_get_primary_keys(), \c odbc_get_foreign_keys(), \c odbc_get_indexes(),
      \c odbc_get_procedures(), \c odbc_get_type_info()
    - fixed bug where \c getOption() returned swapped values for \c login-timeout and \c connection-timeout
    - fixed wrong error message when setting invalid \c connection-timeout option
    - fixed missing return statements after validation errors in \c setOption()
    - fixed \c assert() instead of proper null check in \c odbc_get_driver_real_name()
    - added columnar DBI result support with \c Datasource::selectColumnar() and
      \c SQLStatement::fetchColumnar() when built against %Qore with columnar DBI APIs
    - optimized columnar DBI results to return dense buffers for integer, floating-point,
      and safe \c SQL_NUMERIC / \c SQL_DECIMAL columns

    @subsection odbcv1_1_3 odbc Driver Version 1.1.3
    - fixed handling retrieving 0-length \c VARCHAR values
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4681">issue 4681</a>)

    @subsection odbcv1_1_2 odbc Driver Version 1.1.2
    - update to fix builds with the updated \c qpp from %Qore

    @subsection odbcv1_1_1 odbc Driver Version 1.1.1
    - fixed a bug iterating result sets with the \c SQLStatement class
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4616">issue 4616</a>)
    - fixed handling character encoding issues; strings are bound and retrieved using the DB encoding for the
      datasource; eliminated special logic for handling UTF-16 strings that caused crashes in some cases
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4615">issue 4615</a>)
    - fixed a bug where the \c conn option would be used to build the connection, but the value was not returned as an
      option value
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4613">issue 4613</a>)

    @subsection odbcv1_1 odbc Driver Version 1.1
    - automatically strip trailing spaces from \c CHAR column values
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4508">issue 4508</a>)
